      <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
      <p class="name">David S. Jones</p>
      <p>I've spent more than twenty-five years as a consultant in technology and cybersecurity, and more than fifty as a believer in Christ. I'm a member of Scottsdale Bible Church, where I serve on the worship teams and serve in the men's group, The Forge, helping to disciple men and pointing them to Jesus. Trained in classical music at Northern Arizona University; father of two, Austin and Izzy.</p>
      <p>My heart is for service and for evangelism &mdash; helping ordinary people meet the God whose forgiveness has no limit. That's what this site is: a table set every week, for anyone who wants to sit down. And since 2026 it's also where I <a href="/coaching/">coach and mentor men</a> one-to-one and <a href="/speaking/">speak</a> to churches and men's groups.</p>
      <p>I lost a job at fifty-eight, walked into the Phoenix Seminary library, and came out with Matthew 18 and a book. Divorced, rebuilt, forgiven. If you're somewhere in the middle of that sentence, you're who I write for.</p>
    </div>
